  "summaries": {
    "en": "House selection, skill certification routing, battalion management, and recruitment strategy for all four routes of Fire Emblem: Three Houses.",
    "ja": "学級選択、技能習得ルーティング、バタリオン管理、全4ルートの加入戦略を解説するファイアーエムブレム 風花雪月攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "strategy-rpg",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1599930113854-d6d7fd521f10?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Teaching efficiency during monastery phases determines unit quality for the entire playthrough—focus instruction time on each unit's certification-required skills, not their natural strength stats, to unlock advanced classes 3–4 chapters earlier.",
      "Battalions provide effective Combat Arts and regenerate between battles at the unit's own expense—keep battalion endurance above 30% before major battles; a depleted battalion loses its gambits, which are often the most reliable crowd control option.",
      "The Dancer certification (requires Riding D or higher) is available to any female character from Chapter 9 onward—unlocking Dancer on a support unit provides the Turn 2 double-action that wins most 5-star difficulty battles.",
      "Recruiting students from other houses costs Professor Level (increased by teaching and activity points) and minimum skill levels—prioritise recruiting Petra (Blue Lions), Lysithea (Black Eagles), and Leonie (Blue Lions) before Chapter 12 when cross-house recruitment closes.",
      "New Game Plus carries over all Professor Level, support ranks, and unit skill progress—second playthroughs on Hard/Maddening can be started with maximum Professor Level, enabling full recruitment within the first 5 chapters."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "修道院フェーズの指導効率がプレイスルー全体のユニット品質を決める。自然な強みステータスではなく、上級職認定に必要な技能への指導時間を集中させ、3〜4章早く上級職を解放する。",
      "バタリオンは戦闘技と勝利ボーナスを提供し、ユニット自身のコストで戦闘間に回復する。大戦前にバタリオン耐久を30%以上に保つ。枯渇したバタリオンはガンビットを失い、最も信頼できる制圧手段が消える。",
      "ダンサー認定（騎術D以上が必要）は第9章以降に全女性キャラが受験可能。サポートユニットのダンサー解放は2ターン目の2アクションを提供し、難易度☆5の多くの戦闘を勝利に導く。",
      "他学級からの加入は教授レベル（指導と活動ポイントで上昇）と最低技能レベルが必要。第12章で学級間加入が終了する前に、ペトラ（青獅子）・リシテア（黒鷲）・レオニー（青獅子）の加入を優先する。",
      "ニューゲームプラスは教授レベル・支援レベル・ユニット技能進行を引き継ぐ。2周目以降をハード/魔神難易度で開始する際、最大教授レベルで始めれば第5章以内に全加入が可能になる。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "House Selection Considerations",
        "body": "Each house offers a different story route and playable character pool. Black Eagles (Edelgard route) has the most healing-focused units and the unique ability to access all routes via the \"Edelgard route split\" in Chapter 11. Blue Lions (Dimitri route) has the strongest physical unit composition. Golden Deer (Claude route) offers the most balanced party and is the recommended first playthrough for strategy newcomers. The Ashen Wolves (Church route) requires completing other routes first and is designed as a narrative capstone."
      },
      {
        "title": "Monastery Activity Efficiency",
        "body": "Each month provides 5–7 free activity points plus Professor Level bonuses. Optimise: spend Advice Box points on units who are 1–2 skill points away from certification requirements, not on fully spec'd units. Use Lost Items returns to boost Support levels (support conversations unlock Adjutant slots that double unit effectiveness in later chapters). Gardening and fishing provide statbooster items—allocate at least 2 activity points per month to these passive stat bonuses."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Class Certification Strategy",
        "body": "The Intermediate class tier (Chapters 4–11) provides the highest stat growth rates in the game—stay in Intermediate classes as long as certification allows rather than rushing to Advanced. The optimal path for most combat units: Beginner → Fighter/Myrmidon (max level 20) → Intermediate Brigand (unlocks Death Blow, +6 Attack on initiation) → Advanced class of choice. Death Blow is the most universally valuable Combat Art in the game and worth the 2-month detour for any physical attacker."
      },
      {
        "title": "Paralogue and Mission Order",
        "body": "Paralogues (optional side missions) expire after specific story chapters—Lysithea's Paralogue expires after Chapter 6, Cyril/Alois Paralogues expire after Chapter 12. Completing Paralogues provides unique battalions and Hero's Relics that are significantly stronger than standard equipment. The Sword of Begalta relic (Claude Paralogue, Chapter 6) provides the best bow-range weapon in the first half of the game and is usable by any trained Archer."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Maddening Difficulty Adjustments",
        "body": "Maddening difficulty adds +20% enemy stat growth per level and removes pre-battle convoy access. Key Maddening adaptations: always enter battles with at least 3 gambits available (each battalion must be above 50% endurance before battle), equip Retribution combat art on Adjutant units to trigger counter-attack on enemy-initiated combat, and never use Divine Pulse (rewind) more than 5 times per chapter—strategic retreat and reset is more efficient than exhausting rewinds on lost units."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Investing instruction in skills the unit already has at A-rank—skill ranks above A provide diminishing returns compared to bringing a weak skill from D to B for certification unlocks.",
      "Ignoring the Adjutant system—Adjutants participate in combat at no cost and can learn skills passively from the main unit; placing a Mage Adjutant on a physical unit secretly raises the Adjutant's Magic skill without spending activity points.",
      "Rushing certification to Master class immediately—Master class stat growth rates are lower than Advanced class in most stat categories; spending extra levels in Advanced provides a larger final stat pool.",
      "Missing time-limited supports—certain support conversations expire after specific chapters and are never recoverable without New Game Plus; B-rank supports provide unique conversation scenes unavailable at A-rank.",
      "Not banking battalions before maps with ambush spawns—ambush spawn maps place new enemies at your exposed flanks 3 turns in; keep your flanking units' battalions full before any map with numbered enemy reserves shown in the forecast."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "すでにAランクの技能への指導に時間を使う。Aランク以上の技能レベルはDからBへの認定解放と比べてリターンが低い。",
      "副官システムを無視する。副官はコストなしで戦闘に参加し、メインユニットから受動的にスキルを習得する。物理ユニットに魔法使い副官を配置すれば、活動ポイントを使わず副官の魔力が密かに上がる。",
      "上級職をスキップしてすぐに特級職に認定する。特級職のステータス成長率は多くの項目で上級職より低い。上級職で余分にレベルを積むと最終的なステータスプールが大きくなる。",
      "期限付きの支援会話を見逃す。特定の章後に会話が消えて取り返せない支援会話がある。Bランク支援はAランクで解放されない固有シーンを提供する。",
      "奇襲増援のあるマップ前にバタリオンを温存しない。奇襲増援マップは3ターン目に側面に新たな敵が出現する。マップ予報に敵増援数が表示されている場合、側面ユニットのバタリオンをフルに保つ。"
    ]
